1
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:09,904
Administrator Guide - Users, reviewing questions, building papers, PDFs, paper format and the audit log

2
00:00:09,954 --> 00:00:15,285
Welcome! This video shows everything an administrator does in the SKANS Question Bank.

3
00:00:15,335 --> 00:00:21,243
Teachers write questions; you manage users, review questions, build exam papers and download the PDFs.

4
00:00:21,302 --> 00:00:24,876
Chapter 1: Signing in and the admin dashboard

5
00:00:24,926 --> 00:00:36,640
Sign in with your username and password. The first time, you choose your own password, exactly like teachers.

6
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:47,507
As an administrator you see more in the menu: Review, Papers, Users, Subjects, Paper format and Audit log.

7
00:00:47,557 --> 00:00:55,973
The tiles show questions waiting for review, approved questions, drafts and papers. New question and New paper are at the top.

8
00:00:56,023 --> 00:01:01,645
Recent papers, recent activity and a table of questions per subject complete the overview.

9
00:01:01,717 --> 00:01:06,678
Chapter 2: Managing users

10
00:01:06,728 --> 00:01:17,305
Users lists everyone. Use the buttons to show only admins, teachers, Research Officers or inactive accounts.

11
00:01:17,355 --> 00:01:22,349
To add someone, click Add user.

12
00:01:22,399 --> 00:01:32,312
Type the full name and a username: small letters and numbers, for example sara.ahmed.

13
00:01:32,362 --> 00:01:37,160
Choose the role: Teacher, Research Officer or Administrator.

14
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:46,057
Tick the subjects this person may write for. Teachers only see their own subjects.

15
00:01:46,107 --> 00:01:57,839
Give a temporary password. Send it to the person; they must choose their own at the first sign-in.

16
00:01:57,889 --> 00:02:03,837
Each row has buttons. The pencil edits name, role, subjects or Active.

17
00:02:03,887 --> 00:02:15,159
The key resets a forgotten password: a new temporary password appears. Copy it and send it to the person.

18
00:02:15,209 --> 00:02:22,934
After five wrong passwords an account locks for 15 minutes. The open-lock button unlocks it at once.

19
00:02:22,984 --> 00:02:30,725
The power button deactivates someone who left. They cannot sign in, but their work is kept.

20
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:36,695
Tip: keep two administrator accounts, so you can never be locked out of the system.

21
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:41,608
Chapter 3: Subjects

22
00:02:41,658 --> 00:02:48,144
Subjects shows the eight CAF papers in Group A and Group B. They are set up already.

23
00:02:48,194 --> 00:03:00,380
The pencil changes a subject’s name or CAF number. Add subject creates a new one if ever needed.

24
00:03:00,549 --> 00:03:05,404
Chapter 4: Reviewing questions

25
00:03:05,454 --> 00:03:15,100
Review lists every question teachers have submitted. Click a title to read the full question.

26
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:27,027
If the question is good, click the tick to approve it. You can add a note for the author.

27
00:03:27,077 --> 00:03:40,165
If something must change, click the cross to return it. A comment is required, so the teacher knows what to fix.

28
00:03:40,215 --> 00:04:09,908
Only approved questions can be used in papers. Let us approve the rest quickly.

29
00:04:09,993 --> 00:04:15,617
Chapter 5: Questions as administrator

30
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:22,465
As administrator you see all questions of all teachers, including their drafts, and you can edit any question.

31
00:04:22,515 --> 00:04:30,620
The same filters, search, preview and recycle bin work here. You can also write questions yourself with New question.

32
00:04:30,684 --> 00:04:35,681
Chapter 6: Building a paper: details

33
00:04:35,731 --> 00:04:42,690
Papers lists all exam papers. The demo paper is here already. Click New paper.

34
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:50,124
Details: give the paper a title and choose the subject.

35
00:04:50,174 --> 00:04:59,234
Session, exam date, maximum marks, duration and reading time print in the paper’s heading.

36
00:04:59,284 --> 00:05:08,974
Prepared by: the teacher, Research Officers and admin. These names print only in the answer key.

37
00:05:09,024 --> 00:05:17,503
Instructions come from the paper format. Custom for this paper lets you change them for this paper only.

38
00:05:17,564 --> 00:05:22,986
Chapter 7: Building a paper: questions

39
00:05:23,036 --> 00:05:31,545
On the left are the approved questions of this subject. Search to find a topic.

40
00:05:31,595 --> 00:05:43,414
Click a title to read the question first. Add to paper puts it in the paper.

41
00:05:43,464 --> 00:05:54,133
Or simply click the plus button next to a question.

42
00:05:54,184 --> 00:06:02,951
On the right is the paper in order. The arrows move a question up or down; the cross removes it.

43
00:06:03,001 --> 00:06:12,165
Choose the section for each question, change its marks for this paper, or start it on a New page.

44
00:06:12,215 --> 00:06:19,743
At the top right you always see the total marks against the maximum.

45
00:06:19,815 --> 00:06:23,400
Chapter 8: Preview and saving a draft

46
00:06:23,451 --> 00:06:34,750
Preview shows the question paper exactly as it will print.

47
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:43,864
Scroll to check it. Use maximise for a bigger view. Close it when done.

48
00:06:43,914 --> 00:06:51,089
Click Save. The paper is saved as a draft and can be changed any time.

49
00:06:51,144 --> 00:06:55,938
Chapter 9: Downloading drafts for review

50
00:06:55,988 --> 00:07:01,031
Download has the question paper and the answer key as PDF files.

51
00:07:01,081 --> 00:07:11,604
While a paper is a draft, every page says DRAFT - FOR REVIEW. Share drafts for checking before finalising.

52
00:07:11,654 --> 00:07:21,487
Tick this box to print your name and the time on every page, so a leaked copy can be traced.

53
00:07:21,537 --> 00:07:32,926
Preview key shows the answer key with model answers, examiner’s advice and the names.

54
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,570
Chapter 10: Finalising the paper

55
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:46,449
Finalise is only possible when the total marks equal the maximum marks. Let us set the maximum to the total.

56
00:07:46,499 --> 00:07:52,321
Now the total matches, and Finalise is enabled. Click it.

57
00:07:52,371 --> 00:08:06,942
A final paper is frozen: later changes to its questions do not change it. Downloads are now clean, without DRAFT.

58
00:08:06,992 --> 00:08:11,743
Both PDFs are downloaded: the question paper and the answer key.

59
00:08:11,806 --> 00:08:15,399
Chapter 11: Versions and reopening

60
00:08:15,449 --> 00:08:29,868
History lists every saved version. Restore brings an older version back as a new draft; nothing is deleted.

61
00:08:29,918 --> 00:08:44,043
Need to change a final paper? Reopen turns it back into a draft. The final version stays in the history.

62
00:08:44,131 --> 00:08:49,128
Chapter 12: The paper library

63
00:08:49,178 --> 00:08:56,967
The library shows every paper with its status. Search finds a paper by its title.

64
00:08:57,017 --> 00:09:06,705
Duplicate copies a paper as a new draft, for example to make the next mock test.

65
00:09:06,755 --> 00:09:18,292
Delete removes a paper. You are asked to confirm first.

66
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:24,836
Chapter 13: Paper format

67
00:09:24,886 --> 00:09:30,505
Paper format controls how every paper looks: fonts, sizes, spacing, margins, headings and instructions.

68
00:09:30,555 --> 00:09:41,827
Change a value and it is highlighted. The small arrow puts that one value back to the SKANS standard.

69
00:09:41,877 --> 00:09:49,641
Click a section title to open more settings.

70
00:09:49,691 --> 00:10:02,360
Reset to standard puts every setting back at once. Nothing changes until you click Save.

71
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:07,907
Chapter 14: The audit log

72
00:10:07,957 --> 00:10:14,767
The audit log records every sign-in, change, review, PDF download and deletion, with the user and the time.

73
00:10:14,817 --> 00:10:26,807
Filter by user, action, record type or dates to find something quickly.

74
00:10:26,898 --> 00:10:30,891
Chapter 15: Signing out and good habits

75
00:10:30,941 --> 00:10:38,039
Change your password with the key icon at the bottom left. Sign out when you leave a shared computer.

76
00:10:38,089 --> 00:10:45,903
Good habits: one account per person, deactivate people who leave, and keep a second administrator account.

77
00:10:45,953 --> 00:10:52,969
You are ready to run the SKANS Question Bank - Backups run every night. For server questions, see the Server Setup Guide.
